    outlook: "Tokenized equity is likely to gain traction as regulators clarify rules. Companies like Shein may explore tokenization after their IPO to diversify capital, while platforms will need to secure proper licensing to avoid legal disputes like AMC’s case.",
    conclusion: "The crypto industry’s failed lobbying bid, AMC’s legal threat over tokenized shares, and Shein’s successful IPO collectively highlight the complex interplay between blockchain innovation and traditional regulatory frameworks. While tokenized equity offers enticing benefits, the path to widespread adoption remains fraught with legal, regulatory, and operational challenges.",
